<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The capability shore ~ mesh owns the shape, adapters prove it

Twenty-nine lines, no dependency, no provider. Keyhive, a local-dev stub, a job handler, a future
UCAN or CAIP or EIP-712 bridge — each satisfies this interface without any of them appearing in the
mesh package, and the mesh reaches none of them by name.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! The invariants

# ''The shape depends on no provider.'' Nothing here imports a concrete authority package, so adding
a provider costs the mesh no edit and removing one breaks no type.
# ''The gate reads BINARY.'' `CapabilityAccess` admits `read` and `admin`, and app-specific policy
narrows from there. A caller that wants a finer verb narrows AFTER this answers, never inside it.
# ''The presenter stays OPAQUE.'' A DID, an account id, a verifying key, a provider handle — the
shape carries a string and interprets none of it. Whoever verifies decides what the identifier means.
# ''A question names three things.'' Who presents, which bag URL, and which access. A verify call
carrying fewer would ask about a principal in the abstract, which no provider can answer.
# ''A refusal MAY explain itself.'' `CapabilityVerifyResult` carries `ok` and an optional `reason`, so
a denial can say why without the boolean losing its meaning. A caller reads `ok` and nothing else.
# ''Verification runs ASYNC.'' A provider may reach a network, a WASM boundary or a disk, and a
synchronous shape would have forced every one of them to lie about it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/what-it-does-not-decide>>

!! What this shore declines to answer

''It never says a principal MAY act, only that a provider vouches for the pair.'' Standing and
capability travel on different axes; a verifier that returned standing would fuse them.

''It never narrows by verb.'' The richer access axis — `pull · read · edit · admin`, mirroring
Keyhive's own verbs — stands as a MODEL at `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/causal-islands`, and no
call site in this tree narrows an action by it. Naming a tier here as though it gated would promise a
reader a check they could then fail to find.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

